Everything matches except: target emits `lui $v1,%hi(func_80166EA8_ovl_30+0x20)` as the 3rd insn, BEFORE `sw $ra,0x14($sp)` and before `lbu 6($s0)`; ours emits it after the lbu. This is exactly proposal #6's known KMC expander/sched1 limitation (target hoists %hi before sw ra, this build cannot). Tried: volatile element table (required; non-volatile folds to $at form and scores much worse), local volatile Fn *tbl, local Fn fn, pointer-to-element `&D[a->x[6]]` — all identical 60. search_flags: all -O2/-O3/-G8 variants 60, -fno-schedule-insns 120, -O1 330; flags are not the issue. No C shape found that moves the %hi up. Remaining fix needs the proposed split-address/scheduler KMC build.

Cannot get closer than 60: this is exactly proposal #6's known KMC-build blocker, verified again. Best source (score 60, 35/35 insns, only 2 reordered rows):
Obj={u8 x[0x2D8];}; typedef void(*Fn)(Obj*,s32,s32);
extern volatile Fn D_80166738_ovl_35[];
void func_8016492C_ovl_35(Obj*a,s32 b,s32 c){
  D_80166738_ovl_35[a->x[6]](a,b,c);
  if(a->x[6]!=3) func_80089D34_ovl_01(a,b,c,0x100);
  *(u16*)(a->x+0x2D0)=*(u16*)(a->x+0x1E0);
  *(u16*)(a->x+0x2D2)=*(u16*)(a->x+0x1E2);
  *(u16*)(a->x+0x2D4)=*(u16*)(a->x+0x1E4);
}
Target has `lui $v1,%hi(func_80166730_ovl_17+0x8)` between `sw $s2` and `sw $ra`; this build always emits it after `sw $ra` and after `lbu 6($s0)`. Tested since last release: `u8 st=a->x[6]` index local (60, no change); explicit byte-pointer arithmetic `(*(volatile Fn*)((u8*)D + (a->x[6]<<2)))(...)` (550, folds to $at); try_compiler -fschedule-insns2 (60), -fno-schedule-insns2 (545), -fno-delayed-branch (330). Plain non-volatile table is much worse. Everything else in the function already matches byte-for-byte, including the three u16 copies. Only the proposed split-address/scheduler KMC build can fix the %hi placement.

Best score 90/53 insns, only prologue scheduling differs (5 rows). Use this C (it got 90):

typedef struct { u8 x[0x2D0]; } Obj;
extern s32 func_80032DEC_ovl_01(Obj *, s32, s32, s32);
extern s32 func_8008A974_ovl_01(Obj *, s32, s32, s32);
void func_801633AC_ovl_14(Obj *a, s32 b, s32 c) {
    switch (a->x[6]) {
    case 0:
        *(volatile s32 *)(a->x + 0x1E8) = 0x06000F00;
        *(volatile u8 *)(a->x + 0x2CE) = 4;
        t = *(volatile u16 *)(a->x + 0x2C8);
        s = *(volatile u8 *)(a->x + 6);
        *(volatile u16 *)(a->x + 0x2C8) = t | 2;
        *(volatile u8 *)(a->x + 6) = s + 1;
    case 1:
        p = *(Obj **)(a->x + 0x2C4);
        if (p != 0)
            func_80032DEC_ovl_01(a, *(s32 *)(p->x + 0x28), *(s32 *)(p->x + 0x30), 0x20);
        if (func_8008A974_ovl_01(a, b, c, 0x10100) != 0) {
            *(volatile u8 *)(a->x + 0x2CE) = 3;
            t2 = *(volatile u16 *)(a->x + 0x2C8);
            *(volatile s32 *)(a->x + 4) = 0x01050000;
            *(volatile u16 *)(a->x + 0x2C8) = t2 & 0xFFFD;
        }
        break;
    }
}
(locals u16 t; u8 s; u16 t2; Obj *p declared at top or inside cases; both score 90. The explicit volatile u16 t2 load is required for lhu before the sw 4(s0) and makes the constant use $v1.)

REMAINING 5-row diff: target prologue is sw s0 / addu s0,a0 / sw s1 / addu s1,a1 / sw ra / sw s2 / lbu v1 / beqz / addu s2,a2. KMC emits sw s0 / addu s0,a0 / sw ra / sw s2 / sw s1 / lbu v1 / addu s1,a1 / beqz / addu s2,a2. Everything after that matches byte for byte. b/c are copied to s1/s2 only because they must survive the func_80032DEC call (the matched sibling func_80163480_ovl_16 has no such call, and passes a1/a2 straight through - that's why it matches).

Tried and no effect: locals declared inside case vs at top; src copies s32 bb=b, cc=c; u8 st=a->x[6] then switch(st). Tried the "two if (st==0) ... if (st==1)" form: much worse (1160). This family (func_80166550_ovl_11 in ovl_11) has the identical issue; autopilot stuck at 150 there. Suspect sched2 tie-break ordering of the prologue register saves/moves: need a source shape that makes the a1->s1 copy be emitted earlier in RTL (before the ra/s2 saves). Worth trying declaration-order permutations or an alias for b whose assignment lands before the switch.

Best stored 570 (autopilot m2c); my best manual attempt 580. My source (580) is a switch on a->x[6]:
case0: u16 t = *(volatile u16*)(a->x+0x2C8); *(volatile s32*)(a->x+0x1E8)=0x04000F00; *(volatile u8*)(a->x+0x2CE)=3; *(volatile u16*)(a->x+6)=0x100; *(volatile u16*)(a->x+0x1F4)=0; *(volatile u16*)(a->x+0x2C8)=t&0xFFFD; /* fallthrough */
case1: if (func_8008A974_ovl_01(a,b,c,0x100)!=0){ u8 s=*(volatile u8*)(a->x+6); *(volatile s32*)(a->x+0x1E8)=0x04000300; *(volatile u8*)(a->x+6)=s+1; } break;
